WEBVTT

NOTE Captions match the narration. Times follow the spoken words.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.380
Keep the project goal, instructions
and durable facts together.

2
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.340
Instructions guide future turns.

3
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.100
They do not replace a
provider's native history.

4
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.010
Memory belongs to this project.

5
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.330
Open a file to review its contents.

6
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:27.040
Give a lasting decision its
own small Markdown file.

7
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.450
Save the decision.

8
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.810
SpecWithCode checks the file
revision before replacing it.

9
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:42.050
Reload and reopen the file to
confirm that the decision persisted.

10
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.710
A different project keeps a
different memory collection.

11
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.560
Usage comes from recorded provider turns.

12
00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.520
Missing data remains visible.

13
00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.070
No provider turn ran in this walkthrough.

14
00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:05.750
An equivalent cost estimate is not a bill.
